  "interpretation": [
    "18 experiments completed;9 adoption gates fail. Completion is not a qualification pass. CLI exit2 is intentional for unmet gates.",
    "Connection-local fixture marker avoids H2 leading-comment callback truncation. SQL text, parameters and fixture nonce are not logged.",
    "The stale-before-request client witness uses an adversarial direct JDBC cache bypass; it is not a supported production writer.",
    "The supported native Admin REST writer also commits disable before the paused request resumes; that request still returns enabled state. Its writes share the unmarked SQL channel and cannot be attributed to the observer.",
    "Other tagged JDBC windows record zero unmarked protected row attempts and zero unmarked mutating/unknown prepared-command starts. This does not cover every SQL attempt.",
    "Repeated model/query reads can retain cached or managed entities. Late rebind/delete/recreate can return the earlier association. These reject latest-state-at-response/revalidation claims; they do not alone define or refute every possible linearizable point-in-time contract.",
    "A fresh/atomic/version/fencing contract covering observation and later token acquisition must be decided and qualified before adoption. No existing acceptance is weakened.",
    "Callbacks observe prepared command execution, zero-row DML, rollback and nested DDL. A client-rejected parse-time failure is not visible in these H2 server callbacks; pre-command, abrupt-death, broader delayed effects and other statement coverage remain unqualified.",
    "Observer pauses occur inside the real database before/after queries. Deliberate fixture commits/rollback and forced death affect only new synthetic state; no authenticated result or query result is injected.",
    "Actual database loss during the query returns generic no-store503; restart/recovery preserves protected fingerprints and a fresh native retry succeeds. This is not general provider transaction rollback, cluster or PostgreSQL qualification."
  ],
